@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@ package, not for somebody reading this repository's commit log.
 
 ### Added
 
+- `list_conversations` and `conversation_list` WebSocket frames (`ListConversationsMessage`, `ConversationCursor`, `ConversationSummary` and `ConversationListMessage`, exported from the package root) so a connected client can list the authenticated user's conversations over the socket it is already authenticated on: `{sessionId, createdAt, updatedAt, entryCount}` with ISO-8601 timestamps, newest first, paged with `limit` and `before`. The list is always the connection's own user's — a client-supplied `userId` is ignored — and it is answered only when asked, never pushed. Opt in with `transport: {history: {enabled: true}}`; the default is off, and with it off the frame is answered with an `error` frame carrying the new `UNSUPPORTED` code, as it is when your session store implements no `listFor` or refuses the list by throwing the also-new exported `StoreCannotList`. A `listFor` that fails any other way answers `SERVER_ERROR` and leaves the socket open. Enable `transport.resume` alongside: a listed conversation is reopened with `?sessionId=<id>`, which only resume reads — the engine logs a warning at startup when history is on without it.
 - `SessionStore.listFor(userId, options?)`, an optional store member that answers the summaries of a user's conversations — `sessionId`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt` and `entryCount` — most recent activity first, so a consumer can build a conversation list instead of only rejoining one. Nothing in the engine calls it yet: the store answers the list, and the route or frame that carries it to a client is still yours to write. `InMemorySessionStore` and `MongoSessionStore` both implement it; a store of your own may leave it out. A summary never carries a conversation's entries or its credentials. Page with `limit` (50 by default, 200 at most, and `0` answers nothing) and `before`, which takes the last summary you saw: the cursor carries both `updatedAt` and `sessionId`, so two conversations saved in the same millisecond cannot straddle a page boundary and go unlisted. See `docs/session-stores.md` § Listing a user's conversations.
 
 ### Changed
